      "problem": "Determine the quotient and remainder of $6x^3-x^2+3x+1$ divided by $3x^2+x+2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,2x-1 \\\\  & 3{x}^{2}+x+2\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,6{x}^{3}-\\phantom{0}{x}^{2}+3x+1\\,\\,} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{6{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4x}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-3{x}^{2}-x+1 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,3{x}^{2}-x-2}_{―} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n- the quotient is ${\\color{blue}2x-1},$ and\n\n- the remainder is ${\\color{red}3}.$",
